{
  "conversation_lines": [
    {
      "turn_number": 1,
      "time": "2143-10-21 14:30:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "Hello, Mr. Johnson. I’m Dr. Lee, one of your hospital doctors. You’ve been admitted today because your pacemaker battery is running low and the leads are showing higher thresholds. You’re here for a procedure to replace it with a new leadless pacemaker called a Micra."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 2,
      "time": "2143-10-21 14:32:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "Okay, doctor. I’ve had this pacemaker in my abdomen for years. Is it safe to remove it?"
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 3,
      "time": "2143-10-21 14:34:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "Yes, it’s a planned procedure. The abdominal generator will be removed, and the new Micra device will be placed through your right leg vein directly into your heart. It doesn’t need wires, so it’s less invasive."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 4,
      "time": "2143-10-21 14:36:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "That sounds better. But I’ve had infections before with my fistula. Could this cause another infection?"
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 5,
      "time": "2143-10-21 14:38:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "We’re aware of your history, especially with MRSA and MSSA. That’s why we’ll give you antibiotics during the procedure and a short course afterward to prevent infection."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 6,
      "time": "2143-10-21 14:40:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "Good. And what about my diabetes and kidney transplant? Will this affect those?"
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 7,
      "time": "2143-10-21 14:42:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "We’ll monitor your kidney function and blood sugar closely. Your tacrolimus levels were checked this morning and are within range. We’ll keep your insulin and transplant meds on schedule."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 8,
      "time": "2143-10-21 14:44:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "I’ve been feeling a bit nauseous lately. Is that from my gastroparesis?"
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 9,
      "time": "2143-10-21 14:46:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "Yes, gastroparesis is common with your type 1 diabetes. We’ll manage that with small meals and medication if needed. We’ll avoid anything that could slow your stomach further."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 10,
      "time": "2143-10-21 14:48:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "Alright. When will the procedure happen?"
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 11,
      "time": "2143-10-21 14:50:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "Tomorrow morning. Tonight, we’ll run some final checks—blood work, EKG, and a chest X-ray to confirm current device position."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 12,
      "time": "2143-10-21 14:52:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "Okay, thanks. I’m a little nervous, but I trust you."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 13,
      "time": "2143-10-21 14:54:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "That’s completely understandable. We’ll be with you every step. Rest well tonight."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 14,
      "time": "2143-10-22 08:15:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "Good morning. You’re doing well. Your labs are stable, and the chest X-ray confirms your current pacemaker leads are in place. The procedure is scheduled for 9 AM."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 15,
      "time": "2143-10-22 08:17:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "Great. Any last-minute instructions?"
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 16,
      "time": "2143-10-22 08:19:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "We’ll stop your blood thinners briefly. You can take your other morning meds with a sip of water. The team will take you shortly."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 17,
      "time": "2143-10-22 13:30:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "Hi, you’re back from the procedure. Everything went well. The Micra was successfully placed in your right ventricle, and your old abdominal generator was removed."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 18,
      "time": "2143-10-22 13:32:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "That’s a relief. I remember waking up with some pain in my back and groin."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 19,
      "time": "2143-10-22 13:34:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "Yes, you had some bleeding at the groin site when you coughed after extubation. We held pressure for 15 minutes and used a FemStop device. No hematoma formed, and the site is now stable."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 20,
      "time": "2143-10-22 13:36:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "I felt really nauseous too. Is that normal?"
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 21,
      "time": "2143-10-22 13:38:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "Yes, it’s likely from a combination of your gastroparesis, the long anesthesia time, and the pain medication—Dilaudid. We gave you Zofran, and you’re doing better now."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 22,
      "time": "2143-10-22 13:40:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "I couldn’t pee either. That scared me."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 23,
      "time": "2143-10-22 13:42:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "We scanned your bladder and found 700 cc of urine. We put a temporary catheter in, but you’ve voided on your own since it was removed. That’s a good sign."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 24,
      "time": "2143-10-22 13:44:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "Good. So my heart is pacing normally now?"
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 25,
      "time": "2143-10-22 13:46:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "Yes, the Micra is working perfectly. Your rhythm is stable, and you’re not having chest pain, shortness of breath, or dizziness."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 26,
      "time": "2143-10-22 13:48:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "And my back pain?"
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 27,
      "time": "2143-10-22 13:50:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "That’s likely from lying still during the long procedure. We’ll manage it with mild pain meds. It should improve quickly."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 28,
      "time": "2143-10-22 13:52:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "Okay. What about my heart failure? I’ve been short of breath lately."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 29,
      "time": "2143-10-22 13:54:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "Your ejection fraction is 40%, which means your heart is weaker than normal. The chest X-ray shows mild fluid buildup, so we’ll keep an eye on your weight and continue your usual meds—Lasix, carvedilol, and others."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 30,
      "time": "2143-10-22 13:56:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "I’ll keep weighing myself every morning like my nurse taught me."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 31,
      "time": "2143-10-22 13:58:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "Exactly. Call us if you gain more than 3 pounds in a day. Now, you’re eating and drinking small amounts, which is great. Keep that up."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 32,
      "time": "2143-10-23 09:00:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "Good morning. You look much better. Vital signs are stable, your groin and abdominal sites are healing, and labs are normal."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 33,
      "time": "2143-10-23 09:02:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "I feel better. When can I go home?"
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 34,
      "time": "2143-10-23 09:04:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "Today. We’ll discharge you in a few hours. You’ll go home with a chair car for safety since you shouldn’t drive yet."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 35,
      "time": "2143-10-23 09:06:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "What meds do I need to take?"
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 36,
      "time": "2143-10-23 09:08:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "All your usual meds—insulin, tacrolimus, blood pressure pills, and aspirin. Plus, a 5-day course of cephalexin to prevent infection at the procedure sites."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 37,
      "time": "2143-10-23 09:10:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "And my follow-up?"
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 38,
      "time": "2143-10-23 09:12:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "See the device clinic in one week. They’ll check the Micra. Keep your other appointments for transplant, diabetes, and heart failure."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 39,
      "time": "2143-10-23 09:14:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "I’ll write that down. Thank you, doctor. I appreciate everything."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 40,
      "time": "2143-10-23 09:16:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "You’re welcome. Take care of those wounds—keep them dry and clean. Call us if you have fever, swelling, or trouble breathing. Have a safe trip home."
    }
  ],
  "summary": {
    "admission_start": "2143-10-21 14:19:00",
    "admission_end": "2143-10-23 16:30:00",
    "summary_paragraph": "A male patient with a complex medical history including type 1 diabetes, kidney transplant, chronic systolic and diastolic heart failure, complete heart block, and prior infections was admitted for replacement of a failing abdominal pacemaker generator. He underwent successful explant of the abdominal device and implantation of a Micra leadless pacemaker via the right femoral vein. Post-procedure, he experienced transient groin bleeding managed with manual pressure, intractable nausea attributed to gastroparesis and opioid use, and temporary urinary retention requiring catheterization. He recovered well, tolerated oral intake, ambulated without issue, and was discharged home with prophylactic antibiotics, activity restrictions, and follow-up in the device clinic. His heart failure and transplant medications were maintained throughout.",
    "problems": [
      "Encounter for checking and testing of cardiac pacemaker pulse generator [battery]",
      "Atrioventricular block, complete",
      "Hypertensive heart and chronic kidney disease with heart failure and stage 1 through stage 4 chronic kidney disease, or unspecified chronic kidney disease",
      "Type 1 diabetes mellitus with diabetic chronic kidney disease",
      "Chronic kidney disease, unspecified",
      "Chronic combined systolic (congestive) and diastolic (congestive) heart failure",
      "Kidney transplant status",
      "Long term (current) use of insulin",
      "Atherosclerotic heart disease of native coronary artery without angina pectoris",
      "Personal history of sudden cardiac arrest",
      "Nausea",
      "Low back pain",
      "Other secondary pulmonary hypertension",
      "Paroxysmal atrial fibrillation",
      "Cardiomyopathy, unspecified",
      "Type 1 diabetes mellitus with diabetic autonomic (poly)neuropathy",
      "Gastroparesis",
      "Type 1 diabetes mellitus with diabetic nephropathy",
      "Type 1 diabetes mellitus with unspecified diabetic retinopathy without macular edema",
      "Type 1 diabetes mellitus with diabetic neuropathy, unspecified",
      "Hypothyroidism, unspecified",
      "Other chronic pain",
      "Gastro-esophageal reflux disease without esophagitis",
      "Old myocardial infarction",
      "Personal history of nicotine dependence"
    ]
  }
}
